# Graphify snapshots are immutable and content-addressed. Two branches either
# add distinct paths or add byte-identical content at the same path. If a hash
# invariant is ever violated, fail closed instead of text-merging JSON.
graphify-out/snapshots/** -merge
graphify-out/cache/semantic-cas/** -merge
graphify-out/graph.json merge=graphify

# Snapshots are machine-generated and never read as a textual diff. A promotion
# that prunes superseded snapshots deletes millions of generated JSON lines at
# once, which is large enough that GitHub stops computing the pull request diff
# (the REST API reports 0 changed files) and the code scanning pull request
# check times out waiting on it. Treating them as generated binary keeps the
# same commits and the same change detection while bounding diff cost.
# Safe for the control plane: its promotion patches exclude graphify-out/** and
# are generated with `git diff --binary --full-index`, which is unaffected here.
graphify-out/snapshots/** -diff linguist-generated
